{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795700027,"nonce":"I970Oq+3NAwrbWQFc+Lx58bFBzE=","title":"run_adaptive_solve returns None when criterion= is given","message":"`fem.solve(adapt=jno.solve.remesh(criterion=...))` returns `None` instead of the solution on the adapted mesh.\n\n**What goes wrong.** In `jno/utils/solver/fem_adapt.py`, `run_adaptive_solve` builds the vertex view lazily: `_needs_view = spec.criterion is None or spec.anisotropic`, `u = _vertex_view(...) if _needs_view else None`. This was added so a criterion needs no vertex view (a multifield problem would be refused by `_vertex_view`). But the function returns `u` at the end (\"Returns the solution on the final adapted mesh\"), and for a criterion without `anisotropic=True` it is `None` in every round. The caller's FEM is rebound to the adapted state and `adapt_history` is set, so the adaptation itself works; only the return value is lost. Existing criterion tests (tests/test_fem_adapt_constraint.py) call `fem.solve(adapt=...)` and ignore the result, so none sees it.\n\n**Reproduce.**\n```\nd = jno.shape.rect(0, 0, 1, 1, size=0.15).domain()\n... Poisson form `fem` ...\nout = fem.solve(adapt=jno.solve.remesh(criterion=lambda dm: jno.le(dm.cell_aspect(), 10.0), max_iters=2))\nprint(out)   # None\n```\nMeasured on main (CPU): `type(out)` is `NoneType`. The same call with no `criterion=` returns the vertex values.\n\n**Expected.** The call returns the solution on the final mesh, as the docstring and the no-criterion path do. A `None` where a field is expected fails later, far from the cause, or gets plotted as nothing.\n\n**Where.** jno/utils/solver/fem_adapt.py `run_adaptive_solve` (the `_needs_view` lines and the final `return u`); `FEM.solve` in jno/_fem.py returns it unchanged.\n\n**Workaround.** Read the field from the rebound FEM after the call (`fem.solve()` once more on the adapted mesh), or compute the vertex view yourself.\n\n**Direction.** Compute the vertex view once, after the last round, on the final mesh and return it; keep it lazy inside the loop for the multifield case. Return the full solution vector where `_vertex_view` refuses. Add a test asserting the returned array length equals the final mesh size for a criterion run.","files":null}]}